            <ArticleTitle>Multiple giant aneurysms of coronary arteries.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>55-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Multiple giant aneurysms of the coronary arteries occur extremely rarely and are usually associated with Kawasaki disease in children. A 53-year-old man with multiple giant coronary artery aneurysms was treated successfully by aortocoronary bypass grafting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
